"""NORA intent labelling (v8).

Gives every row of a file an Intent-L2 and an Intent-L4. Every row is read and treated the same way, whatever
produced it. Intent-L1 and all original columns are left untouched; two columns are added.

The domain knowledge (L2 / L4 names, telco phrasing rules, mapping onto any earlier label scheme) lives in
intent_taxonomy.json. Everything else (thresholds, models, new categories) is learned and measured from the data.

Train:  python intent_l2_l4_pipeline_v8.py --input data.xlsx
Score:  python intent_l2_l4_pipeline_v8.py --mode score --model <outdir>/model/intent_model.joblib --input new.xlsx
"""

